back**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Both later versions, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, are marked unhealthy.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Repeating a rollback to the same version is safe, so I ran it once more and it finished in every region.\n- Now: us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, healthy, with the error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident INC-0001 (SEV2)**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n- It covers what went wrong, what I did and the current state.\n\n**Still to do (listed in the incident)**\n- Find out why v2.3.1 fails health checks.\n- Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway.", "type": "text"}]}]}